  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 323 AM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nThe upper level trough responsible for the Short Term's interesting \nweather departs by Wednesday morning, leaving drier conditions and \ncold temperatures in its wake. Freeze products may be necessary for \nmost of the CWA early Wednesday morning as temperatures fall to the \nmid 20s to the upper 30s (near the Rio Grande). Weak upper ridging \ndevelops over our area Wednesday into Thanksgiving, allowing \nafternoon highs to rebound generally into the 50s. A warming trend \ncontinues through the weekend, with highs in the 60s and 70s \nreturning by Saturday. In contrast to the Short Term period, the \nLong Term looks remain dry. However, long-range models have been \nconsistent in showing an upper level low developing over \nnorthwestern Mexico late this week and into the weekend. As of now, \nthis system looks to stay too far south to produce any major impacts \nfor our area, but it may be worth monitoring trends through the next \nseveral days.",
